From 8a52bfa98b90b73e2b96c3c9d981eab7a85300f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:50:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 229/252] feat(execution): promote view_mode=require behind a
 machine-checkable alias proof

- add pypto.alias: contract-view-obligation, stride/shape expressibility,
  write-after-read, owner/lifetime and multi-view-overlap proof chain with
  per-condition status/code/reason and a recomputable digest
- add LayoutPolicy(view_mode=forbid|prefer|require, allow_materialize_copy,
  max_copy_bytes) to ExecutionPolicy; require fails closed with
  ALIAS_PROOF_UNAVAILABLE and the failed conditions, never a silent copy;
  prefer materializes explicitly when proof is missing and budget allows
- land alias_proof/view_obligation/materialize fields in ExecutionPlan and
  ExecutionReport with fail-closed schema checks
- AVX-512 native layout: disabled -> proof_gated; proven reshape views return
  the source buffer while rejected views stay on the bit-identical copy path;
  caller-owned and output/input-aliased storage are rejected explicitly
- SVE256 declares alias_proof=unsupported and supported_view_modes=[forbid,
  prefer] with a user-visible reason (Python-list materialization and
  non-retained TypedByteView exports)
- tests: proof conditions, three-state semantics, adversarial WAR/release/
  output-alias/overlap/chained-view cases, AVX-512 bitwise identity
